&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Everpure (NYSE: P) has evolved from storage pioneer to data platform, closing fiscal 2026 with $3.7 billion in revenue, its first billion-dollar quarter, and accelerating growth into FY27. Our strategic agenda spans the companies defining the next era of technology - hyperscalers, AI labs, the AI hardware supply chain, data platform providers, and the broader AI ecosystem.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This type of work—work that changes the world—is what the tech industry was founded on. So, if you&#39;re ready to seize the endless opportunities and leave your mark, come join us.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;THE ROLE&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Everpure, Inc. (formerly Pure Storage) is adding a Systems (Presales) Engineer to our Commercial district in France, covering the PACA region from Marseille or Aix-en-Provence.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a field presales role for someone with 5+ years of hands-on SE experience who enjoys owning a territory. You will partner with several Account Executives across a mixed portfolio: large regional accounts where you drive the technical agenda, public-sector organizations in health, social services and heavy industry, and a long tail of mid-sized companies where speed and pragmatism win.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHAT YOU&#39;LL DO&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the technical relationship across your territory: discovery, architecture, demos, proofs of concept and technical closure, on Everpure&#39;s Enterprise Data Cloud platform.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take the initiative in large accounts: build activity, find new use cases, and create opportunities rather than wait for them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sell outcomes, not boxes: position services and consumption models (Evergreen//One, storage-as-a-service) credibly with IT and finance stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work day to day with your Account Executives and with channel partners in the region.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own technical responses to RFPs and RFIs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to a national SE team that shares knowledge and wins across districts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHAT YOU BRING – REQUIRED&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years in a field presales / Systems Engineer / Solutions Engineer role, ideally with a territory or multi-account scope.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid general infrastructure culture: compute, virtualisation, networking, data protection, and how they fit together in real customer environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience selling services, subscription or consumption models: you can explain the commercial side as well as the technical one.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A senior, autonomous way of working: you take initiative, drive activity in large accounts, and manage your own agenda.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Curiosity: you learn new technology quickly and like finding new use cases for it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Based in or near Marseille / Aix-en-Provence, with a driving licence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluent French and professional English.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;NICE TO HAVE&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enterprise storage experience (SAN, NAS, object, data protection). Valuable, not required: a dedicated onboarding quarter covers it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background at an infrastructure, data-protection or open-source vendor, or at a services company.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Existing relationships with IT teams in the PACA region.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;LOCATION &amp;amp; TRAVEL&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Home-based in the Marseille / Aix-en-Provence area.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expect to be with customers around half your time or more. Travel is regional, so you are home in the evening, with occasional trips to Paris for team meetings.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHAT YOU CAN EXPECT FROM US:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Innovation&lt;/strong&gt;: We celebrate those who think critically, like a challenge, and aspire to be trailblazers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Growth&lt;/strong&gt;: We give you the space and support to grow along with us and to contribute to something meaningful. We have been named Fortune&#39;s Best Workplaces in Technology™, Fortune&#39;s Best Workplaces in the Bay Area™, and certified as a Great Place to Work®!&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Team&lt;/strong&gt;: We build each other up and set aside ego for the greater good.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;And because we understand the value of bringing your full and best self to work, we offer a variety of perks to manage a healthy balance, including flexible time off, wellness resources, and company-sponsored team events. Check out &lt;a href=&quot;http://benefits.everpuredata.com/&quot;&gt;http://benefits.everpuredata.com/ &lt;/a&gt;for more information.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ACCOMMODATIONS AND ACCESSIBILITY:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Candidates with disabilities may request accommodations for all aspects of our hiring process. For more on this, contact us at &lt;a ---------- if you’re invited to an interview.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;OUR COMMITMENT TO A STRONG AND INCLUSIVE TEAM:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re forging a future where everyone finds their rightful place and where every voice matters. Where uniqueness isn’t just accepted but embraced. That’s why we are committed to fostering the growth and development of every person, cultivating a sense of community through our Employee Resource Groups and advocating for inclusive leadership.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Everpure is proud to be an equal opportunity employer. We do not discriminate based upon race, religion, color, national origin, sex (including pregnancy, childbirth, or related medical conditions), sexual orientation, gender, gender identity, gender expression, transgender status, sexual stereotypes, age, status as a protected veteran, status as an individual with a disability, or any other characteristic legally protected by the laws of the jurisdiction in which you are being considered for hire.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: center;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Join us and bring your best.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: center;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bring your bold.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: center;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pure and simple.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr">Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;p&gt;Notre équipe Digital Repair recherche un·e &lt;strong&gt;Quality Engineer&lt;/strong&gt; (f/m/d) en CDI basé·e à Lille (Campus).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;L&#39;équipe Digital Repair a pour mission de prolonger la durée de vie de nos produits sportifs grâce à des solutions numériques innovantes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Composée de profils variés et passionnés (développeurs, product managers, designers), notre équipe relève le défi de l&#39;économie circulaire chez Decathlon.&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;En nous rejoignant, tu auras un impact direct sur la réduction de notre empreinte écologique tout en offrant une expérience de réparation fluide, fiable et accessible à nos utilisateurs à travers le monde.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;TA FUTURE CONTRIBUTION&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;En tant que Quality Engineer (f/m/d), tu seras le/la garant·e de la qualité des produits que nous mettons à disposition de nos utilisateurs. Tes missions principales seront :&lt;br&gt;* Accompagner les équipes de développement dans la mise en place et le maintien de l&#39;automatisation des tests.&lt;br&gt;* Proposer et ajouter de nouvelles méthodes de test pour toujours garantir un plus haut niveau de qualité tout en réduisant les temps de delivery.&lt;br&gt;* Diffuser la culture de la qualité au sein de l&#39;équipe et collaborer étroitement avec les développeurs dès la phase de conception.&lt;br&gt;* Suivre les indicateurs de qualité et assurer la fiabilité globale de nos parcours utilisateurs.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;CE QUE TU APPORTES&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;* Tu as une expérience solide et confirmée en test d&#39;applications Web et de micro-services.&lt;br&gt;* Tu maîtrises l&#39;usage de l&#39;Intelligence Artificielle (IA) appliquée au métier de la QA pour optimiser et innover dans tes méthodes de test.&lt;br&gt;* Tu es reconnu·e pour ton esprit de synthèse, ta rigueur et ta capacité à évangéliser les bonnes pratiques de qualité.&lt;br&gt;* Tu sais t&#39;intégrer et collaborer efficacement dans un environnement agile.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;STACK TECHNIQUE&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;* Automatisation et tests : Playwright, JEST, Karate&lt;br&gt;* Suivi et gestion : JIRA&lt;br&gt;* Intégration continue (CI) : GitHub Actions&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;CE QUE NOUS T’OFFRONS&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;* Organisation de travail hybride ;&lt;br&gt;* Matériel fourni en accord avec tes missions et nos engagements sociétaux (Mac ou Windows) ;&lt;br&gt;* Une équipe de projet locale au sein d&#39;un réseau mondial (possibilité de carrière internationale) ;&lt;br&gt;* Développement des compétences et accompagnement (diversité des projets, formations internes et externes, etc.) ;&lt;br&gt;* Package de rémunération (actionnariat salarié, bonus mensuels/trimestriels).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;NOTRE ENGAGEMENT EN FAVEUR DE L&#39;INCLUSION ET DE L&#39;ACCESSIBILITE&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;Chez Decathlon, nous reconnaissons l&#39;immense valeur qu&#39;apporte la diversité à nos équipes et nous nous efforçons continuellement de favoriser et de cultiver un lieu de travail inclusif et équitable : c&#39;est pourquoi l&#39;Inclusion est l&#39;un de nos Fondamentaux Humains. Nous encourageons les personnes de tous horizons et de toutes capacités à postuler, car nous sommes convaincu·es que la diversité des pensées, des cultures, des identités et des expériences vécues nous rend plus fort·es.&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;Decathlon s&#39;engage également à offrir un processus de sélection inclusif et accessible à tous les candidat·es. En cas de besoin d&#39;aménagement, tu peux en faire la demande via le formulaire de candidature, celle-ci sera confidentielle. Ces demandes n&#39;affectent pas le résultat du processus de recrutement.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;DECATHLON DIGITAL CONTEXT&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;What if technology allowed us to push the boundaries and take sports experiences to new levels? That&#39;s exactly our goal at Decathlon Digital! We are a team of 5,000+ experts in software engineering, product management, data, cloud, and cybersecurity, distributed across Paris, Lille, and Amsterdam. Together, we are creating the largest digital sports platform, leveraging tech innovation from design to value chain optimization, connected experiences and product second life.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Changing the game for good&lt;/strong&gt;. We are in this for the love of sports. And like everything we love, we want it to last. That’s why we are embarking on a journey to create a more sustainable tech model, reducing our direct environmental impact while maintaining a safe, diverse, and inclusive space for all our people to learn and thrive together. Team up with us to design the digital future of sports.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr">Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;h1&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Product Manager - Categories (f/m/d)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location:&lt;/strong&gt; Paris, France&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Domain:&lt;/strong&gt; E-Commerce Solutions — Navigate &amp;amp; Categories&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ABOUT DECATHLON &amp;amp; THE E-COMMERCE DOMAIN&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Decathlon is accelerating its digital transformation with the mission of becoming &lt;strong&gt;the sports digital platform&lt;/strong&gt; that allows customers to discover our universe through local, sport-centered, and omnichannel experiences.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Mission:&lt;/strong&gt; Bring people together through sport to make wellbeing accessible for all.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;By joining this scope, you will work within the &lt;strong&gt;E-Commerce Solutions&lt;/strong&gt; domain. Our teams build and transform the global e-commerce navigation, catalog treeviews, and backend categorization engines aiming to allows users to effortlessly discover and access Decathlon’s complete offering of products, services, and information&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;JOIN THE CATEGORIES SQUAD&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Reporting to the &lt;strong&gt;Group Product Manager (E-Commerce / Navigate)&lt;/strong&gt;, you will take ownership of the &lt;strong&gt;Categories&lt;/strong&gt; squad. You will work alongside a dedicated engineering squad (Tech Lead, Senior Software Engineers), and collaborate closely with UX Researchers, Product Designers, Data Analysts, Sports Digital Merchandisers, and local Country E-Commerce teams).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Product Vision:&lt;/strong&gt; Empowering discovery through intelligent, scalable navigation. We build an intuitive, automated, and personalized browsing journey so every customer finds what they need, want, and desire faster.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Drive global conversion and incremental revenue by transforming fragmented local treeviews into a unified, high-performing Core Navigation across web and mobile platforms.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;RESPONSIBILITIES&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Product Vision &amp;amp; Strategy&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define the product vision, strategy, and roadmap for the &lt;strong&gt;Categories &amp;amp; Core Navigation&lt;/strong&gt; ecosystem.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own and arbitrate key product streams across &lt;strong&gt;Core Navigation&lt;/strong&gt; (standardizing category trees globally) and &lt;strong&gt;SKU-Level Categorization Engines&lt;/strong&gt; (such as our streaming engine &lt;em&gt;Tesseract&lt;/em&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Align stakeholders across central sports teams, global digital merchandising, and local country teams around shared treeview operating models.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Discovery &amp;amp; Governance&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Continuously identify user, SEO, and market opportunities through data analysis, user testing, and card-sorting studies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish a continuous and consistent A/B testing process to refine business convictions and identify top growth opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Balance global standardization with local market flexibility, ensuring smooth migration from local catalog treeviews to global &lt;strong&gt;Core Trees&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish clear decision-making frameworks and SLAs for global taxonomy, SEO content guidance, and category creation governance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Delivery &amp;amp; Technical Alignment&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead agile product delivery in close partnership with the Engineering Lead and squad members.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prioritize and mature the team’s backlog (epics, user stories) to support multi-level export feed pipelines, batch orchestration tooling, and taxonomy rules execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee key migration milestones for countries adopting the Core Navigation framework across desktop and mobile.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Data &amp;amp; Performance&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and track success metrics across navigation channels, including &lt;strong&gt;PDP Reach Rate, Revenue per Session, Menu Usage CTR&lt;/strong&gt;, and &lt;strong&gt;Category-Level Conversion&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leverage data analytics to streamline category performance, eliminating inactive categories and optimizing taxonomy filters.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Arbitrate and prioritize backlog based on data driven decision&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Product Mindset &amp;amp; Culture&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as an ambassador for product excellence and taxonomy standards across Decathlon’s global network.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Foster a collaborative work environment based on trust, accountability, and user-centric decision-making.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;PROFILE&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience:&lt;/strong&gt; 5+ years of experience as a Product Manager in a fast-paced B2C e-commerce, digital platform, or catalog/search ecosystem.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Domain Expertise:&lt;/strong&gt; Strong understanding of e-commerce navigation, catalog treeviews, taxonomy/metadata structures, or search &amp;amp; discovery platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Stakeholder Management:&lt;/strong&gt; Proven ability to navigate complex, multi-stakeholder international organizations (aligning global tech teams, business merchandisers, and country leads).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Product Methodology:&lt;/strong&gt; Mastery of end-to-end product development—from discovery (UX research, data analysis, A/B testing) to delivery (backlog refinement, technical roadmapping, release planning).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Analytical Mindset:&lt;/strong&gt; Data-driven approach to prioritizing product features and measuring conversion and user experience impact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Language &amp;amp; Communication:&lt;/strong&gt; Fluent in English and French (written and spoken), with excellent synthesis skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Passion:&lt;/strong&gt; Curiosity for solving scalable architecture/data problems, user-centric design, and a strong passion for sports!&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHAT WE OFFER&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Flexible Remote Work:&lt;/strong&gt; 2 days of remote work per week (flexible).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Work Location:&lt;/strong&gt; Based at our Decathlon Technology office in Paris, France.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Choice of Equipment:&lt;/strong&gt; Work on your preferred device (Mac, Windows, Chromebook).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Impact &amp;amp; Career Growth:&lt;/strong&gt; High-impact role at the heart of Decathlon&#39;s global e-commerce engine, offering mentorship, certifications, and international growth paths.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Financial Benefits:&lt;/strong&gt; Employee shareholding opportunities, along with monthly and quarterly performance bonuses.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;DECATHLON DIGITAL CONTEXT&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;What if technology allowed us to push the boundaries and take sports experiences to new levels? That&#39;s exactly our goal at Decathlon Digital! We are a team of 5,000+ experts in software engineering, product management, data, cloud, and cybersecurity, distributed across Paris, Lille, and Amsterdam. Together, we are creating the largest digital sports platform, leveraging tech innovation from design to value chain optimization, connected experiences and product second life.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Changing the game for good&lt;/strong&gt;. We are in this for the love of sports. And like everything we love, we want it to last. That’s why we are embarking on a journey to create a more sustainable tech model, reducing our direct environmental impact while maintaining a safe, diverse, and inclusive space for all our people to learn and thrive together. Team up with us to design the digital future of sports.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr">Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;GitLab is the intelligent orchestration platform for DevSecOps. GitLab enables organizations to increase developer productivity, improve operational efficiency, reduce security and compliance risk, and accelerate digital transformation. More than 50 million registered users and more than 50% of the Fortune 100* trust GitLab to ship better, more secure software faster.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The same principles built into our products are reflected in how our team works: we embrace AI as a core productivity multiplier, with all team members expected to incorporate AI into their daily workflows to drive efficiency, innovation, and impact. GitLab is where careers accelerate, innovation flourishes, and every voice is valued. Our high-performance culture is driven by our values&amp;nbsp;and continuous knowledge exchange, enabling our team members to reach their full potential while collaborating with industry leaders to solve complex problems. &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=OuZIb5zszQI&quot;&gt;Co-create the future with us&lt;/a&gt; as we build technology that transforms how the world develops software.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;*&lt;em&gt;Fortune 500® is a registered trademark of Fortune Media IP Limited, used under license. Claim based on GitLab data. Fortune 100 refers to the top 20% ranked companies in the 2025 Fortune 500 list, published in June 2025. Fortune and Fortune Media IP Limited are not affiliated with, and do not endorse products or services of GitLab.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;The SMB New Business Account Executive role is a critical role in building GitLab’s customer-base and continued long-term growth. The SMB New Business Account Executive will focus exclusively on acquiring new customers and generating new logos by executing on an inbound/outbound sales playbook.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role, you will own a territory and book of prospect accounts (including free GitLab users, trials, engaged leads and cold prospects). You will navigate it by leveraging data, developing a deep understanding of the product, the market, customer challenges and business needs. You will strategically build relationships with your accounts and lead a consultative sales cycle by painting the vision of DevSecOps with GitLab and helping them achieve business outcomes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a high-impact role for someone who is competitive, self-starter and hungry, who is excited by forming new motions, thrives in a hunter environment and is energized by building relationships and business cases from scratch.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive selling into free users and base prospects within the SMB segment by articulating the value of GitLab. Engaging with inbound prospect and proactively reaching out to prospects showing potential and key signals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build, co-create and consistently iterate on the outbound / new logo playbook and strategy to win new customers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Introduce and execute against new creative prospecting and campaign ideas&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take ownership of and act as the CEO for the book of business in your territory:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Document the buying criteria &amp;amp; process, next steps &amp;amp; owners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and execute comprehensive prospecting strategies to build and maintain a healthy pipeline of new business opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work and collaborate with our Partner ecosystem to drive new business and value for our customers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Utilize business and industry knowledge to research accounts, identify key players, generate interest, create/identify compelling events, and develop accounts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage the full sales cycle from initial contact to close by involving technical audience, multiple stakeholders and decision-makers, and articulating GitLab’s value proposition to across various industries&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Master MEDPICC and Command of the Message on all opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with cross-functional teams including Sales Development, Solution Architecture and Digital Marketing to develop winning strategies in targeting accounts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to root cause analyses on wins/losses.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communicate lessons learned to the team, including the marketing team, the technical team and product&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Feedback: Effectively communicate learnings, feedback and challenges to relevant teams (including Product Development, Sales, and Marketing) to drive continuous improvement, and be the voice of the prospect by contributing product ideas to our public issue tracker&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to documenting improvements in our sales handbook&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Market knowledge: Maintain a foundational understanding of technologies related to GitLab’s market focus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Training &amp;amp; Certifications: Acquire industry standard certifications to build up credibility as a technical expert&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Performance Metrics&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Achieving monthly and quarterly new logo acquisition targets, for both new logo count and booked ARR&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You share our values, and work in accordance with those values&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A self-starter with a proven track record of resilience, motivation and results&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated track record of outbound sales activity, securing calls, meeting and winning business, with a creative ability to break into new accounts and build business cases&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Effective communicator, strong interpersonal skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent discovery skills, ability to uncover and address customer pain points, negotiation, presentation and closing skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated progressive experience in sales, technical consulting, customer success, marketing, or customer service in the field of information technology&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An understanding of B2B software, Open Source software, and the developer product space is preferred&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with modern sales tech stack including Salesforce, Clari, Outreach, ZoomInfo/Cognism, LinkedIn Sales Navigator, Gong, and 6sense&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Basic understanding of application lifecycle management including the technology commonly used in application lifecycle management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be ready to learn how to use GitLab and Git&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Focuses on continuously improving your professional skills with a focus on personal mastery and team learning through activities such as training, reading and seeking mentorship from others&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in another language ie. French, German, Spanish, Dutch&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to travel if needed and comply with the company’s travel policy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;#LI-CM1&lt;/p&gt;
